{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness","id":1533820,"title":"Looking for ideas for the Patriarch\u2019s weakness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-08T09:01:16-07:00","id":1533820,"title":"Looking for ideas for the Patriarch\u2019s weakness?","content":"So I want to build a high level game where there is a chance my niece and her friends get to kill the Patriarch\u2019s equivalent of a Maeljin Incarna. Obviously, the Patriarch\u2019s representative is an old, bearded, blue eyed white guy.<br /> <br /> What weaknesses does the Patriarch have? What is the secret bane that will kill his Incarna\u2019s embodiment? Beating him to death with a signed copy of \u201cThe God Delusion?\u201d Having a woman who is also a lesbian drive a frozen tampon through his heart? Poison him with a mixture made with the powdered bones of a woman who won a Nobel Prize in science?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I know there was a similar thread nearly a year ago, but I never got ideas on how to kill him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-08-2024, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:24:40-07:00","id":1533825,"title":"","content":"The Patriarch <i>is</i> the Patriarch's equivalent of a Maeljin. As a Weaver-spirit, it probably has proscriptions against admitting its own fallibility or acknowledging its inner contradictions (such as outline by George Carlin; &quot;... but he loves you!&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:26:38-07:00","id":1533826,"title":"","content":"I thought the Patriarch was just a Weaver aspect and Maeljin Incarna are beings that used to be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:32:18-07:00","id":1533827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1533826#post1533826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Patriarch was just a Weaver aspect and Maeljin Incarna are beings that used to be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm works differently on account of being bound by the Weaver. A Weaver-spirit that simply happens to be an Incarna can just do Incarna things and doesn't rely on a vessel as such, though it probably does need a lot of adherents to go to bat for it, else it couldn't very well be a powerful manifestation of Dogma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T10:56:58-07:00","id":1533828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1533827#post1533827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wyrm works differently on account of being bound by the Weaver. A Weaver-spirit that simply happens to be an Incarna can just do Incarna things and doesn't rely on a vessel as such, though it probably does need a lot of adherents to go to bat for it, else it couldn't very well be a powerful manifestation of Dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always interpreted it as a cool trick the Wyrm came up with to funnel Malfeas and its corruption into the physical world. And since it deals in the physical world, the Weaver should also be capable of the feat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T11:39:54-07:00","id":1533830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1533828#post1533828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always interpreted it as a cool trick the Wyrm came up with to funnel Malfeas and its corruption into the physical world. And since it deals in the physical world, the Weaver should also be capable of the feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a cool trick that the Wyrm came up with... under duress. It's not actually likely that the Weaver can copy it; it's kind of like how the Weaver can keep spinning up webs, but remains vulnerable to the corruption of the Defiler Triatic Wyrm, which specifically targets the webs that the Weaver relies on so that it can ride them to one destination or target or another. Meanwhile, the Weaver remains pretty much helpless against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:26:43-07:00","id":1533834,"title":"","content":"My presumption would be that the most-dramatically satisfying way to defeat The Patriarch (or avatar of same) would be to persuade someone groomed from birth by the old villain to not only renounce him but Denounce him: bringing together those who have been his victims together to drive him off - whether with blows or mockery - would certainly be classically heroic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:46:27-07:00","id":1533852,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s some spitballing on the concept<br /> <br /> it really depends on how you want to play \u2018the Patriarch\u2019 in your chronicle, what they represent. Even in canon, you could go with the Patriarch as representing the Dogma aspect of the Weaver, the incarna representing a patrilineal usurpation of a preceding mother-right, or the Werewolf spiritual counterpart to a PIE Sky-Father type mythic archer (if one doesn\u2019t place Grandfather Thunder in that type of role). <br /> <br /> In the first case, the Weaver case, I could perhaps see a story taking inspiration from various schools of thought which have developed in the backlash to centralized hierarchal religious organizations: perhaps the key to the defeat of the Patriarch-as-Dogma is the dissolution of the concept of a universal notion in favor of absolute subjectivity, a sort-of Nietzchean Crowleyite doctrine of all people being the masters of their own subjective authorities without relation to one another or any external benchmark. If, however, this is a bit too much of a radical individualist interpretation, maybe then the issue is not Dogma-as-such, ie Dogma as common or universal notions shared by multiple people, but rather the particular Dogmas which predominate. In that case perhaps one goes on a quest to undermine the particular dogmas of the Patriarch and, once suitably weakened, initiate a ritual to reform the Patriarch into a more desirable form with more suitable/desirable dogmas at their core.<br /> <br /> The second interpretation would be particularly interesting to the Black Furies (as well as potentially the Red Talons, certain Children of Gaia, certain OB &amp; YB, certain BG, etc.). This Patriarch is part of a spiritualized narrative which depicts a historical struggle between the predominance of mother-right (matrilineal, matrifocal, matriarchal, etc.) and that of father-right (patrilineal, patrifocal, patriarchal, etc.). This narrative sees the rise of the father-right as ultimately a usurpation, a negation of the prior liberties of the mother-right, and the institutional of patriarchy in the ur-form of \u2018woman and children as possessions of the husband-father\u2019. This has economic, social, spiritual, religious, and cultural implications. The Black Furies, more than any other tribe, are concerned with reversing the usurpation and reinstating the primordial laws and customs associated with the era of the mother-right. They might be joined by others who view the development of father-right, patriarchy as core to the corruption of Weaver, Wyrm, and its consequences. Examples may include: Red Talons who see in the Patriarch a seed of the later agrarian lifestyles which necessitated the extirpation and eradication of wolves (amongst other children of the Wyld), Children of Gaia sympathetic to the BF position, Bone Gnawers who liken the Patriarch to the forces of hierarchical organization of power and resources which places them and their kin at the bottom of the social order (if not entirely rejected from the social order), members of Older Brother (Ghost Council) &amp; Younger Brother (Gale Stalkers) who, setting aside the unique systems of socio-sexual politics in the pre-Columbian Americas, identify the role played by the Patriarch in the ideology and logic of settler-colonial expansion. That one can imagine an ideologically motivated resistance arising to this form of the patriarch is not difficult, but how to defeat it? One could go many ways, but perhaps through some combination of sabotaging the structural bases for the patriarch as it currently exists alongside the reintroduction and propagation either of the mother-right and/or the propagation of some new mode to replace both father-right and mother-right.<br /> <br /> For the third concept, this one is relatively simple and may be more easily adopted by the more traditional tribes (Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Fenrir, Fianna, etc.) if one so chooses. There\u2019s plenty of precedent in the mythology surrounding Sky-Fathers for their usurpation by their child-rivals. In this case perhaps we see a Dune-style mission to identify candidates to become the Child Usurper figure who can overthrow and replace the Patriarch under some new form, whether \u2018the Conquering Son\u2019 or something else entirely. Perhaps one could even use the Perfect M*tis for a role of this nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T16:34:06-07:00","id":1533860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1533852#post1533852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here\u2019s some spitballing on the concept<br /> <br /> it really depends on how you want to play \u2018the Patriarch\u2019 in your chronicle, what they represent. Even in canon, you could go with the Patriarch as representing the Dogma aspect of the Weaver, the incarna representing a patrilineal usurpation of a preceding mother-right, or the Werewolf spiritual counterpart to a PIE Sky-Father type mythic archer (if one doesn\u2019t place Grandfather Thunder in that type of role).<br /> <br /> In the first case, the Weaver case, I could perhaps see a story taking inspiration from various schools of thought which have developed in the backlash to centralized hierarchal religious organizations: perhaps the key to the defeat of the Patriarch-as-Dogma is the dissolution of the concept of a universal notion in favor of absolute subjectivity, a sort-of Nietzchean Crowleyite doctrine of all people being the masters of their own subjective authorities without relation to one another or any external benchmark. If, however, this is a bit too much of a radical individualist interpretation, maybe then the issue is not Dogma-as-such, ie Dogma as common or universal notions shared by multiple people, but rather the particular Dogmas which predominate. In that case perhaps one goes on a quest to undermine the particular dogmas of the Patriarch and, once suitably weakened, initiate a ritual to reform the Patriarch into a more desirable form with more suitable/desirable dogmas at their core.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve read Book of the Wyrm W20, and to be clear, I want a struggle against a Patriarch that is akin to a Maeljin Incarna. Or maybe just a being that is the human embodiment of the Patriarch. The way Lord Steel is an embodiment of Abhorra.<br /> <br /> I like the Wyrm\u2019s Maeljin Incarna and I want to fight a Weaver version of one. Specifically, the most toxic aspect of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T12:57:27-07:00","id":1534264,"title":"","content":"Might be worth reading in the Kult game for ideas. One of the Death Angels in that, Chagidiel (the Bloodstained Patriarch) occupies much the same symbolic space as the WtA Patriarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T13:47:10-07:00","id":1534531,"title":"","content":"The Patriarch can only truly be defeated when GW starts making female Space Marines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T15:36:23-07:00","id":1534533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1534531#post1534531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Patriarch can only truly be defeated when GW starts making female Space Marines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any way to elaborate on this? I don't understanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T19:32:39-07:00","id":1534536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1534533#post1534533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any way to elaborate on this? I don't understanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s just a joke, based on Games Workshop\u2019s 40K wargame where some people want female Space Marines and others want them to be exclusively make. It kinda falls down along feminist vs anti-feminist lines - which is why I joked about the Patriarch. <br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean for anybody to take it seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T19:38:33-07:00","id":1534537,"title":"","content":"For the record, I don\u2019t play Warhammer, but I know what Space Marines are and I think they should be allowed to be female.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T08:20:17-07:00","id":1534556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1534536#post1534536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s just a joke, based on Games Workshop\u2019s 40K wargame where some people want female Space Marines and others want them to be exclusively make. It kinda falls down along feminist vs anti-feminist lines - which is why I joked about the Patriarch.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean for anybody to take it seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard about this, there were a handful of people complaining, but what exactly is the problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T07:23:58-07:00","id":1534633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1533820-looking-for-ideas-for-the-patriarch\u2019s-weakness?p=1534537#post1534537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I don\u2019t play Warhammer, but I know what Space Marines are and I think they should be allowed to be female.</div> </div> </div> </div> Give us a new Sisters of Battle codex and associated miniatures, then we\u2019ll talk.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}